# 13 — Cursor Implementation Guide — Telos

> Supplements `MASTER_PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md`, `docs/10_AI_Rules.md`, and `docs/11_AI_Prompt_Library.md`. Does not replace them. Defines how Cursor (or any implementation tool operating in this role) must behave for the lifetime of the Telos project.
>
> **Format note:** rules are stated as `MUST` / `MUST NOT` / `SHOULD` (RFC 2119-style), one directive per line, each with a rule ID (`CIG-x.x`) and a cross-reference to the doc section that governs it. This is deliberate — it's written to be parsed and cited by an AI tool, not just read by a human.
>
> **Renumbered from the submitted draft's "12"** — `12_Roadmap.md` already occupies that slot. This document is `13`.

